==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|emphatick}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰeh₂-|id=shine}}
From {{der|en|grc|ἐμφατικός||emphatic}}, from {{m|grc|ἐμφαίνω||I show, present}}, from {{m|grc|ἐν||in}} + {{m|grc|φαίνω||I shine, show}}; related to {{m|grc|ἔμφασις}} and English {{m|en|emphasis}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪmˈfætɪk/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-emphatic.wav|Audio (UK)}}
* {{a|weak vowel}} {{IPA|en|/əmˈfætək/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ætɪk|s=3}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Characterized by [[emphasis]]; [[forceful]].
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=June 28, 2012
|author=Jamie Jackson
|title=Wimbledon 2012: Lukas Rosol shocked by miracle win over Rafael Nadal
|work=the Guardian
|url=http://www.guardian.co.uk/sport/2012/jun/28/rafael-nadal-lukas-rosol-wimbledon-2012?INTCMP=ILCNETTXT3487
|page=
|passage=Yet when play restarted the [[Czech]] was a train that kept on running over Nadal. After breaking Nadal in the opening game of the final set, he went 2-0 up and later took the count to 4-2 with yet another '''emphatic''' ace – one of his 22 throughout.}}
# Stated with [[conviction]].
#: {{ux|en|He gave me an '''emphatic''' no when I asked him out.}}
# {{lb|en|grammar}} Belonging to a set of English tense forms comprising the auxiliary verb [[do]] + an infinitive without [[to]].
# {{lb|en|phonology}} Belonging to a series of [[obstruent]] [[consonant]]s in several [[Afro-Asiatic]] languages that are distinguished by a [[guttural]] [[coarticulation|(co-)articulation]].
#: {{ant|en|plain}}
## [[pharyngealized]] consonants in [[Arabic]], [[Hebrew]], other Northwest Semitic languages, and [[Berber]] languages
## [[ejective]] consonants in [[Ge'ez]], [[Amharic]], other Ethiopic Semitic languages, [[Chadic]] and [[Cushitic]] languages
# {{lb|en|phonology|archaic|_|except in layman’s use}} Referring to the above consonants as well as {{w|Voiceless pharyngeal fricative|{{IPAchar|/ħ/}}}} and {{w|Voiced pharyngeal fricative|{{IPAchar|/ʕ/}}}} (these being seen as emphatic equivalents of {{w|Voiceless glottal fricative|{{IPAchar|/h/}}}} and {{w|Glottal stop|{{IPAchar|/ʔ/}}}}).

